 {"id":"fabro-e505","title":"engine: honor run.integrations.github token grants ONLY for User-principal runs — agent-authored config must never mint credentials (ADR-0019.6)","status":"closed","type":"bug","priority":0,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T22:44:13.872Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T06:52:33.419Z","assignee":"agent","description":"ESCALATION CHAIN (user analysis 2026-09-08): the line's agents WRITE their own workflow configs (.fabro/workflows/** via PRs) - so an agent could add [run.integrations.github] permissions and the engine would mint a write-capable GITHUB_TOKEN into its own sandbox env (self-escalation + exfiltration). Per ADR-0019.6 the config possibility itself must go.\n\nCLOSED 2026-09-08 with full acceptance evidence:\n1. Implementation 52fbb843c: capability_gate::gate_github_integration at the run-start seam (server.rs), neutralizing resolved integrations for every non-User principal with a warn naming ADR-0019.6. Unit tests: user keeps, worker denied, system empty.\n2. Wire test 919b0d18c: run_start_grants_github_token_bridge_only_to_user_principals - in-process full-seam proof via HTTP run create + execute_run; capturing wait-node handler asserts User run keeps token bridge + GITHUB_TOKEN in stage env, Worker run (run-tools worker token creator) gets neither. 926/926 suite green, clippy+fmt clean.\n3. Deployed: image 2026-09-08T06:05Z contains the gate (binary string verified in container fabro-fabro-1), container healthy, conductor schedule enabled, on_overlap=skip intact.\nFollow-up filed: fabro-c274 (github_app resolution precedes the gate; no-creds worker runs hard-fail instead of silent no-token - latent availability, fail-closed).","labels":["engine"],"closedAt":"2026-09-08T06:52:33.419Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-0f22","title":"engine: scrub clone token from sandbox remote URL — engine git ops switch to transient per-exec credentials (user decision 2026-09-08)","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T22:44:13.979Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T22:50:21.231Z","description":"USER DECISION 2026-09-08: 'das clone token darf auch nicht zur verfuegung stehen, die remote url wird nach dem clonen nicht gebraucht und ist eine tickende zeitbombe' - option (a) chosen: credential-free sandbox, repo-contents access only (ADR-0019.6).\n\nCURRENT STATE: docker.rs/daytona clone embeds the minted token in the remote origin URL (embed_token_in_url); push_credentials.rs drives engine pushes through EXACTLY that embedded token (compare -> set-url -> record, with re-embed drift recovery at sandbox.rs:1994-1998; daytona rewrites set-url on refresh). Any agent can read it via 'git remote get-url origin' and exfiltrate via curl/web_fetch.\n\nDESIGN (decided): (1) after clone+checkout completes, scrub the remote to the CLEAN https URL ('git remote set-url origin https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>') - the token never persists in repo config; (2) ALL engine-side git network ops (branch push, fetch/refresh, drift recovery) switch to TRANSIENT per-exec credentials: docker_exec_shell already accepts env_vars - pass a GIT_CONFIG overlay (GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/GIT_CONFIG_KEY_x=http.<origin>.extraheader with the basic-auth header) exactly like git_bridge.rs merge_git_bridge_env already builds for shells; the credential exists only in that exec's env, never in repo config, never in agent tool env; (3) the re-embed drift path becomes re-MINT + transient exec instead of set-url; (4) agent-side fetch/pull to origin degrade (they should not need network git - engine does all forge ops); document that in the iterate/agent guidance if a prompt references git pull.\n\nAcceptance: 'git remote get-url origin' in a fresh run container shows the CLEAN url (no token anywhere in config: grep -r x-access-token .git -> empty); engine push/refresh still work (run PRs merge as before, live-verified on the next line pass); no credential reachable from any agent shell or journal; wire tests for push+scrub+transient-exec.","labels":["engine","workflows"],"assignee":"agent"}
 {"id":"fabro-9e49","title":"Make current_seed_brief criteria newline-bulleted in the planner prompt","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T23:11:26.439Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T23:20:30.046Z","description":"Basis: run 01M1Z1PK3D7R9MEWDP7QDZMA1D (seed fabro-cf76). The planner's current_seed_brief (context values, seq 62) crammed all six acceptance criteria into one mashed single line despite .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md step 6 demanding BULLETED criteria; the implementer (seq 107) had to re-split the criteria itself for the PASS/FAIL report — exactly the misparse surface the bullets were meant to remove. Change: in planner.md step 6, require newline-separated bullets (\\n- ) inside the current_seed_brief JSON string instead of one mashed line. Expected effect: clean criterion→PASS/FAIL mapping for implementer and reviewer; fewer ambiguity-driven Changes-requested cycles (~2.5 min + ~$0.15 each per the seed's own estimate). Not a duplicate: existing brief-quality seeds (fabro-ad1b, fabro-b8ed, fabro-fb19) target implementer-side citation or brief content, not planner-side bullet formatting. Cross-refs: fabro-ad1b, fabro-b8ed, fabro-fb19.\nBasis: run 01M1Z1PK3D7R9MEWDP7QDZMA1D, workflow version be58840fab1c246bee538760df54ab8f8bfe6bb0bcf0356df6aaf38d5f14ef20, commit ce495789f5be8fbe233670d0e0c3a72ddd9d4bca","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
-{"id":"fabro-0b41","title":"revisor: scope seed WRITES to its own set — supersession closes and label changes never touch user-owned seeds (ADR-0018)","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T23:16:53.343Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T23:16:53.343Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"USER FINDING 2026-09-08 (revisor prompt review): the revisor's seed WRITE operations are unscoped - the supersession rule (prompts/file.md) says 'a finding SUPERSEDES an existing open seed... file the new seed, then immediately sd close <old-id>' with NO ownership boundary, so the revisor could close USER-owned seeds (design forks like fabro-3b1b, grill topics like fabro-b11a, upstream-posture seeds) and thereby remove items from the user's decision space - an ADR-0018 violation (the revisor owns nothing; reviewing is not owning). READS stay GLOBAL (sd search against the full inventory is correct - duplication is assignment-orthogonal; scoping the search would CREATE duplicates against user-owned work).\n\nFIX (prompts/file.md, sequence AFTER PR #59 which touches the same file): (1) supersession closes ONLY seeds labeled revision (revisor-originated set) or assigned @fabro; user-owned/unassigned seeds are NEVER closed by the revisor - when a finding supersedes one, cross-reference it in the new seed's description and journal 'supersession candidate (user-owned, not closed): <id>' for the human gate; (2) label backfill (--set-labels revision) only on seeds already labeled revision or provably revisor-originated (Basis cites a revisor run); (3) add one sentence to the tracker command reference table: 'ownership rule: close/relabel only your own or @fabro seeds - ADR-0018 D2'. Acceptance: prompt states the ownership boundary; a staged test or journal evidence shows a user-owned supersession candidate is cross-referenced, not closed.","labels":["workflows","revision"]}
