 {"id":"fabro-8be7","title":"parse_auth_logout_all fails when FABRO_SERVER is set (env-dependent unit test)","status":"open","type":"task","priority":3,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:19:31.269Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T06:19:31.269Z","description":"fabro-cli bin test tests::parse_auth_logout_all (lib/apps/fabro-cli/src/main.rs) asserts args.server.server.is_none(), but the --server default resolves from the FABRO_SERVER env var. Fails in shells where FABRO_SERVER is exported (reproduced 2026-09-08, agent session had FABRO_SERVER=http://127.0.0.1:32276); passes with 'env -u FABRO_SERVER cargo nextest run -p fabro-cli --bin fabro parse_auth_logout_all'. Fix: scrub/lock FABRO_SERVER in the test instead of assuming a clean shell. Mulch: testing/parse-auth-logout-all-env-dependent."}
 {"id":"fabro-c274","title":"engine: github_app credential resolution runs BEFORE the ADR-0019.6 gate - non-user runs with permissions-declaring config hard-fail when no GITHUB_TOKEN is configured","status":"closed","type":"bug","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:52:05.704Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T07:09:28.283Z","labels":["engine"],"description":"Found during the fabro-e505 wire test (2026-09-08): github_app resolution ran BEFORE the ADR-0019.6 gate; the is_token_requested() branch hard-failed for EVERY principal when the vault had no GITHUB_TOKEN, making Worker runs with permissions-declaring config unrunnable without credentials.\n\nCLOSED 2026-09-08 (9d1ae6162, direct agent work on explicit user assignment, line stopped): resolve_integration + gate now run BEFORE the credential lookup; the hard-fail branch keys on the GATED integration (empty for non-User principals, so only User principals reach it); agent-side runs fall through to the best-effort clone/pull-request branches and execute credential-free per the e505 spec. Verification: new test worker_principal_run_without_vault_token_takes_no_token_path (empty vault, worker run succeeds, no bridge, no GITHUB_TOKEN in stage env); 927/927 suite green; clippy+fmt clean. Deploy note: lib/ change -> needs the next just up (line stopped; fold into the next deploy window).","assignee":"fabro","closedAt":"2026-09-08T07:09:28.283Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-d43a","title":"workflows: unify the self-reflection journal schema - conductor + merge-upstream stages must emit the standard painpoints/observations shape (prompt fix)","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:56:10.174Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T07:03:10.714Z","labels":["workflows","revision"],"description":"USER FINDING (2026-09-08): the journal the conductor-driven passes produce does not match the standard self-reflection format. ALL workflows must use the SAME self-reflection schema.\n\nCLOSED 2026-09-08, implemented directly by the agent on explicit user assignment (line stopped, ~15 min):\n- 6 prompts now carry the standard schema block VERBATIM (painpoints as [{\"text\": ...}] objects + observations as strings + 'on EVERY pass / silence is a missing report / always emit BOTH keys / \"none\" valid / engine records durably'): merge-upstream merge.md + review.md, conductor survey.md + develop-leg.md + merge-leg.md + revise-leg.md. Role specifics live only in the observation placeholders (merge: upstream count/conflict classes/gate duration; review: touchpoints/time/obsolescence themes; survey: count/subject/revisor backlog; legs: child id/status/gate-wait outcome). The informal 'journal it' call-sites in the procedure bodies now bind to the declared shape.\n- Mechanism: copy-paste (12 blocks total across the 4 workflows), not the TemplateIncludeResolver variant - schema equality was the mandate; the include refactor stays available as follow-up if drift ever appears.\n- stage-journal.nu untouched (schema-agnostic by design). Legacy plain-string painpoint lines stay as-is (not migrated).\n- Verification: validate-workflows.nu green (18/22 zero-diagnostic; the 4 graphs with diagnostics - merge-upstream/develop/revisor/conductor - are pre-existing advisories untouched by this prompt-only diff); each of the 6 files carries exactly one schema block; diff is prompt-only, no binary need.\n- Live proof pending by design: next merge-upstream pass must journal painpoints as [{\"text\": ...}] objects and next conductor pass must carry non-empty survey/leg journal data - verify when the line is re-enabled (conductor was stopped by the user for session end).","assignee":"agent","closedAt":"2026-09-08T07:03:10.714Z"}
